### GET cats
GET {{apiUrl}}/cats
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### GET cat by ID
GET {{apiUrl}}/cats/8

### GET cat by ID (FAIL: not found)
GET {{apiUrl}}/cats/98

### GET cats by user ID
GET {{apiUrl}}/users/37/cats

# cat_name, weight, owner, filename, birthdate

### POST new cat
POST {{apiUrl}}/cats
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "cat_name": "Rolle",
    "birthdate": "2022-10-10",
    "weight": 4,
    "owner": "Tiina",
    "filename": "https://placecats.com/310/240"
}

### POST cat with IMAGE
POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/cats HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=MyBoundary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cat_name"

Misu
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weight"

6
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="birthdate"

2023-10-08
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="dog.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./dog.png
--MyBoundary--

### PUT existing cat
PUT {{apiUrl}}/cats/48
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "weight": 6,
    "cat_name": "Uusi nimi"
}

### DELETE cat by ID
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/cats/48

## /users resource

### Register new user
POST {{apiUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Illia",
    "username": "illia",
    "email": "illia@example.com",
    "password": "1234567"
}


## /auth resource

### User login
# @name login
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "illia",
    "password": "1234567"
}

### Get my user info
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### delete cat by id
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/cats/60
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}